.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt WLCOREPROBE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlcoreprobe
.Nd check the libwayland event loop
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility checks the event loop of
the libwayland-server library.
That event loop is written for Linux epoll, timerfd, signalfd and
eventfd.
MINIX has none of these, so Ixolo emulates them on top of
.Xr poll 2 .
.Nm
drives the real event loop through each emulated part.
It takes no arguments.
.Pp
It checks, in order, that:
.Bl -enum
.It
A file descriptor source fires exactly once when a pipe becomes
readable.
This tests the epoll emulation.
.It
An idle source runs exactly once.
.It
A timer set for 60 milliseconds fires, and not before about
55 milliseconds have passed.
A timer that has been disarmed does not fire.
This tests the timerfd emulation.
.It
A signal source fires when the process raises
.Dv SIGUSR1 .
This tests the signalfd emulation.
.It
A display can be created, can advertise
.Li wl_shm ,
and can create a listening socket, and the socket exists on disk.
.It
.Fn wl_display_run
returns after a timer calls
.Fn wl_display_terminate
100 milliseconds later.
This tests the eventfd emulation.
.El
.Pp
Each check prints one line ending in
.Dq OK
or in
.Dq FAIL
with a reason.
The path of the listening socket is also printed.
The last line is
.Dq ALL PASS
or
.Dq FAILURES PRESENT .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The directory in which the test socket is created.
If it is not set,
.Nm
sets it to
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wayland- Ns Ar N
The test socket.
.Ar N
is the first free number from 0 to 32.
It is removed when the display is destroyed at the end of the run.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 if every check passes, and 1 otherwise.
It stops early, with status 1, if it cannot create the event loop, the
pipe or the display.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wlclient 1 ,
.Xr wlprobe 1 ,
.Xr poll 2 ,
.Xr wlcompd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in Ixolo 0.1.
.Sh BUGS
If the eventfd emulation is broken,
.Nm
hangs in the last check instead of failing.
